WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.049 --> 00:00:21.844
On Thursday Brooklyn nervously watched the Whales play their first opponent in the play-offs: the Loganville Leopards.

2
00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:28.269
The team started off slowly, but the action picked up in the second half, after Dirk and Jacey

3
00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:29.250
rejoined the team.

4
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:35.798
"Phew," she thought when Dirk scored a three-pointer five seconds before the final buzzer.

5
00:00:39.279 --> 00:00:41.180
The Whales won, 59-56.

6
00:00:42.021 --> 00:00:46.263
"Nice win, Whales," Marv said after the game.

7
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.924
"Next we play the Bobcats.

8
00:00:49.564 --> 00:00:53.726
And if the Terriers win their next game, we'll face them again in the final game."

9
00:00:53.746 --> 00:00:55.687
"Oh no."

10
00:00:57.704 --> 00:01:02.048
Everyone groaned at the thought of playing that team with their giant point guard again.

11
00:01:02.068 --> 00:01:04.250
"We'll practice hard!"

12
00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.711
Brooklyn said quickly.

13
00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.313
"We can beat them—Whales Whoosh!"

14
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:15.059
"Whales Whoosh," a few players echoed, but they didn't sound very enthusiastic.

15
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.584
Brooklyn spent Sunday afternoon trying to study for Monday's history test.

16
00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:24.908
She rearranged her note cards and stared at the sky through her window.

17
00:01:30.016 --> 00:01:36.240
It was a cool March day, but the bright sun made it feel like spring Brooklyn couldn't stop

18
00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.480
thinking about the Whales.

19
00:01:38.521 --> 00:01:43.664
She was pretty sure that the Whales could beat the Bobcats, but the Terriers were the best team

20
00:01:43.704 --> 00:01:47.806
in the league; it would take more than the team's usual plays to beat them.

21
00:01:48.947 --> 00:01:53.809
If Dirk would only practice some of Brooklyn's plays, the team might have a shot at winning the

22
00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:55.370
final championship game.

23
00:01:56.351 --> 00:01:56.951
She sighed.

24
00:01:58.696 --> 00:01:59.877
"I need a study break."

25
00:02:01.158 --> 00:02:04.601
Brooklyn pulled on her Whales sweatshirt and basketball sneakers.

26
00:02:09.584 --> 00:02:14.088
She went downstairs to the family room where her father was reading the Sunday newspaper.

27
00:02:14.108 --> 00:02:18.771
"Dad, can I borrow your laptop?"

28
00:02:19.091 --> 00:02:19.612
she asked.

29
00:02:19.632 --> 00:02:22.314
"I want to study some basketball videos."

30
00:02:23.355 --> 00:02:24.916
Her father lowered his newspaper.

31
00:02:26.604 --> 00:02:29.385
"At lunch you mentioned studying for a history test."

32
00:02:29.405 --> 00:02:34.147
"I promise to study World War II after I review some plays."

33
00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.668
"You sure work hard for those Whales."

34
00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:38.689
Mr. Robbins smiled.

35
00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:42.891
"I suppose World War II can wait an hour."

36
00:02:43.551 --> 00:02:46.832
He pulled his laptop from his briefcase and gave it to Brooklyn.

37
00:02:46.852 --> 00:02:50.414
"Please be careful with this."

38
00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:51.414
"I will.

39
00:02:52.015 --> 00:02:53.695
I promise," Brooklyn said.

40
00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:55.016
"Thanks, Dad."

41
00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.723
She took the computer from her father and gripped it in her hands.

42
00:03:01.204 --> 00:03:04.527
She pretended she had glue on her fingers so she wouldn't drop it.

43
00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:08.850
Brooklyn went through the kitchen and headed to the garage.

44
00:03:11.552 --> 00:03:14.695
Mrs. Robbins was stirring a large pot of chili on the stove.

45
00:03:14.715 --> 00:03:19.379
"Mom, would you open the door for me, please?

46
00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.380
I'm going outside to practice."

47
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.302
"Sure, sweetie."

48
00:03:24.022 --> 00:03:25.704
Her mom wiped her hands on a towel.

49
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.883
Her eyes widened at the sight of the computer in Brooklyn's hands.

50
00:03:30.903 --> 00:03:34.586
"You're not playing basketball with Dad's computer!"

51
00:03:34.606 --> 00:03:39.710
"I'm studying some professional and college plays so I can try them out with the Whales."

52
00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.212
"Oh. I see."

53
00:03:42.232 --> 00:03:46.475
Brooklyn's mom opened the kitchen door and followed her into the garage.

54
00:03:50.358 --> 00:03:52.460
She pressed the button to open the big door.

55
00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:04.803
The sun shone brightly in the sky, but the March air chilled Brooklyn's fingers.

56
00:04:04.823 --> 00:04:06.364
"Here, Brooklyn.

57
00:04:06.825 --> 00:04:08.946
Use this for the laptop."

58
00:04:08.966 --> 00:04:12.128
Mrs. Robbins carried out a folding beach chair from the garage.

59
00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.632
She placed it several yards away from the basketball hoop.

60
00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:24.417
"Okay." Brooklyn set the laptop on the chair and ran back into the garage.

61
00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:32.842
She picked up her favorite basketball—a red, white, and blue one that had been a birthday gift last

62
00:04:32.882 --> 00:04:35.523
year. Mrs.

63
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:36.784
Robbins rubbed her hands.

64
00:04:36.804 --> 00:04:40.706
"When you're finished, come in for some chili.

65
00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:44.388
I'll close the garage door so the basketball doesn't hit the car."

66
00:04:44.408 --> 00:04:46.409
"Good idea.

67
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:47.430
Thanks, Mom."

68
00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.431
Brooklyn clicked the keyboard.

69
00:04:50.932 --> 00:04:53.694
First she wanted to watch the video with the loop play.

70
00:04:54.754 --> 00:04:57.676
Maybe she could figure out where it had gone wrong for the Whales.

71
00:04:58.688 --> 00:05:02.511
The more Brooklyn watched the loop-play video, the more excited she got.

72
00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:07.614
The Whales had missed one critical pass in the game versus the Terriers.

73
00:05:08.435 --> 00:05:12.978
If Brooklyn and Marv practiced the loop play with the players, the team could try it again in

74
00:05:13.018 --> 00:05:13.798
the next game!

75
00:05:13.818 --> 00:05:15.920
"This time it'll work!"

76
00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.241
Brooklyn declared.

77
00:05:17.981 --> 00:05:20.363
She began dribbling the basketball to warm up.

78
00:05:23.925 --> 00:05:27.828
Just then a rider on a blue bicycle turned into Brooklyn's driveway.

79
00:05:30.092 --> 00:05:30.752
"Hi, Brooklyn."

80
00:05:30.772 --> 00:05:34.114
"Hey, Jacey," Brooklyn said.

81
00:05:34.134 --> 00:05:35.694
"Want to ride to the park?"

82
00:05:36.095 --> 00:05:36.835
Jacey asked.

83
00:05:37.715 --> 00:05:42.897
Brooklyn shook her head, a little surprised that Jacey was suddenly being friendly to her.

84
00:05:42.917 --> 00:05:45.118
"I'm working on my coaching.

85
00:05:45.638 --> 00:05:48.159
I know what went wrong in the game against the Terriers."

86
00:05:48.179 --> 00:05:49.940
"Me too!"

87
00:05:51.041 --> 00:05:52.341
Jacey laughed loudly.

88
00:05:52.361 --> 00:05:55.022
"You fell and Coach broke his rear!"

89
00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:56.943
"Very funny."

90
00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.164
Brooklyn took a shot at the hoop.

91
00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:05.663
The ball hit the rim and bounced toward Jacey, who quickly parked her bike and ran after the

92
00:06:05.683 --> 00:06:17.529
ball. missed a key pass during the loop play," Brooklyn went on.

93
00:06:17.549 --> 00:06:20.651
"The guard has to wait before going to the net.

94
00:06:21.531 --> 00:06:24.933
The loop play might have worked if Dirk had stayed at center court.

95
00:06:25.614 --> 00:06:27.675
I'll teach the play again at practice tomorrow."

96
00:06:27.695 --> 00:06:32.041
"Dirk won't do it," Jacey said, passing the ball.

97
00:06:32.061 --> 00:06:38.006
"If it helps the team win, he will," Brooklyn said confidently.

98
00:06:39.327 --> 00:06:40.168
Jacey shrugged.

99
00:06:40.188 --> 00:06:42.270
"I'm not so sure about that."

100
00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.752
They dribbled the ball back and forth.

101
00:06:48.535 --> 00:06:51.257
Each girl tried shots from different spots on the driveway.

102
00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.102
Then Jacey stopped playing, holding the ball on her hip.

103
00:06:58.122 --> 00:07:02.101
"Brooklyn, don't take this the wrong way.

104
00:07:02.641 --> 00:07:05.243
But it's not just Dirk who's bothered by your coaching.

105
00:07:06.224 --> 00:07:08.745
Some players think you're acting like a know-it-all."

106
00:07:09.646 --> 00:07:11.067
Brooklyn's face grew hot.

107
00:07:11.087 --> 00:07:13.389
"I'm acting like a know-it-all?"

108
00:07:13.749 --> 00:07:14.249
she thought.

109
00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.972
She was just trying to help Marv while Coach was recovering.

110
00:07:17.992 --> 00:07:19.753
"Do you think that, Jacey?"

111
00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:20.673
she asked.

112
00:07:21.954 --> 00:07:23.335
Jacey glanced at the ground.

113
00:07:23.355 --> 00:07:28.078
"I know you love basketball, but that doesn't mean you're an expert.

114
00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:30.140
You don't even play for the team."

115
00:07:31.128 --> 00:07:32.809
Brooklyn felt her heart pounding.

116
00:07:36.492 --> 00:07:38.133
only want to help the team win.

117
00:07:38.773 --> 00:07:40.735
The Whales could be the league champions."

118
00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:45.398
"Well, you're getting on the players' nerves," Jacey said.

119
00:07:45.418 --> 00:07:48.560
"I'm your friend, so I thought you should know."

120
00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.962
Brooklyn swallowed, unsure what to say.

121
00:07:53.123 --> 00:07:56.245
Then she did the only thing that helped when she was upset.

122
00:07:57.486 --> 00:08:00.628
She grabbed her basketball from Jacey and began dribbling.

123
00:08:07.808 --> 00:08:10.829
She dribbled faster, tuning out Jacey for a moment.

124
00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:14.910
Marv often said he listened to his gut when deciding plays.

125
00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:21.432
Brooklyn didn't want to annoy anyone, but she knew in her gut that she could help the team.

126
00:08:21.452 --> 00:08:24.312
"Okay, Jacey," she said finally.

127
00:08:24.332 --> 00:08:25.953
"Thanks for the advice.

128
00:08:26.473 --> 00:08:27.253
Now watch this!"

129
00:08:28.414 --> 00:08:32.515
Brooklyn tossed the ball high, hoping for a clean shot through the basket.

130
00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:37.216
Instead the ball hit the rim and bounced wide.

131
00:08:40.368 --> 00:08:42.130
"No!" Brooklyn cried.

132
00:08:42.811 --> 00:08:45.173
She ran, but she was too late.

133
00:08:46.074 --> 00:08:49.717
The basketball came down, smashing into the beach chair.

134
00:08:51.519 --> 00:08:54.241
Her dad's laptop crashed to the ground.
